TY  - GEN
ID  - noniterativeroth2
AU  - CROOT, ERNIE
AU  - SISASK, OLOF
TI  - A PROOF OF ROTH’S THEOREM ON ARITHMETIC PROGRESSIONS
AB  - We present a proof of Roth’s theorem that follows a slightly diﬀerent structure to the usual proofs, in that there is not much iteration. Although our proof works using a type of density increment argument (which is typical of most proofs of Roth’s theorem), we do not pass to a progression related to the large Fourier coeﬃcients of our set (as most other proofs of Roth do). Furthermore, in our proof, the density increment is achieved through an application of a quantitative version of Varnavides’s theorem, which is perhaps unexpected.
ER  - 

