TY  - JOUR
ID  - s00453-026-01372-w
AU  - Duppala, Sharmila
TI  - Concentration of Submodular Functions and Read-k Families Under Negative Dependence
DA  - D:20260214
DO  - 10.1007/s00453-026-01372-w
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1007/s00453-026-01372-w
AB  - We study the question of whether submodular functions of random variables satisfying various notions of negative dependence satisfy Chernoff-like concentration inequal- ities. We prove such a concentration inequality for the lower tail when the random variables satisfy negative association or negative regression, partially resolving an open problem raised in ([1]). Previous work showed such concentration results for random variables that come from speciﬁc dependent-rounding algorithms ([2, 3]). We discuss some applications of our results to combinatorial optimization and beyond. We also show applications to the concentration of read-k families [4] under certain forms of negative dependence; we further show a simpliﬁed proof of the entropy-method approach of [4].
ER  - 

