ID  - arxiv-1112.0030v2
AU  - Gukov, Sergei
AU  - Stoˇsić, Marko
TI  - Homological Algebra of Knots and BPS States
DA  - D:20181022
UR  - https://arxiv.org/abs/1112.0030
AB  - It is known that knot homologies admit a physical description as spaces of open BPS states. We study operators and algebras acting on these spaces. This leads to a very rich story, which involves wall crossing phenomena, algebras of closed BPS states acting on spaces of open BPS states, and deformations of Landau-Ginzburg models. One important application to knot homologies is the existence of “colored diﬀerentials” that relate homological invariants of knots colored by diﬀerent representations. Based on this structure, we formulate a list of properties of the colored HOMFLY homology that categoriﬁes the colored HOMFLY polynomial. By calculating the colored HOMFLY homology for symmetric and anti-symmetric representations, we ﬁnd a remarkable “mirror symmetry” between these triply-graded theories.
