TI  - Explicit evaluation of the q -Stokes matrices for certain conﬂuent hypergeometric q -diﬀerence equations
DA  - D:20241203
UR  - https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.02281
AB  - We prove a connection formula for the basic hypergeomtric function nϕn−1 (a1, ..., an−1, 0; b1, ..., bn−1; q, z) by using the q-Borel resummation. As an application, we compute q-Stokes matrices of a special conﬂuent hypergeometric q-diﬀerence system with an irregular singularity. We show that by letting q →1, the q-Stokes matrices recover the known expressions of the Stokes matrices of the corresponding conﬂuent hypergeometric diﬀerential system.
ER  - 

TY  - JOUR
ID  - arxiv-math-9810105v2
AU  - JINHO BAIK, PERCY DEIFT
AU  - JOHANSSON, KURT
TI  - arXiv:math/9810105v2 [math.CO] 26 Mar 1999
DA  - D:20241126
UR  - https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9810105
AB  - The authors consider the length, lN, of the length of the longest increasing subsequence of a random permutation of N numbers. The main result in this paper is a proof that the distribution function for lN, suitably centered and scaled, converges to the Tracy-Widom distribution [TW1] of the largest eigenvalue of a random GUE matrix. The authors also prove con- vergence of moments. The proof is based on the steepest decent method for Riemann-Hilbert problems, introduced by Deift and Zhou in 1993 [DZ1] in the context of integrable systems. The applicability of the Riemann-Hilbert technique depends, in turn, on the determinantal formula of Gessel [Ge] for the Poissonization of the distribution function of lN.
ER  - 

TY  - JOUR
ID  - arxiv-math-9906120v3
AU  - Johansson, By Kurt
TI  - Discrete orthogonal polynomial ensembles and the Plancherel measure
DA  - D:20180907
UR  - https://arxiv.org/abs/math/9906120
AB  - We consider discrete orthogonal polynomial ensembles which are discrete analogues of the orthogonal polynomial ensembles in random matrix theory. These ensembles occur in certain problems in combinatorial probability and can be thought of as probability measures on partitions. The Meixner ensemble is related to a two-dimensional directed growth model, and the Charlier ensemble is related to the lengths of weakly increasing subsequences in random words. The Krawtchouk ensemble occurs in connection with zig-zag paths in random domino tilings of the Aztec diamond, and also in a certain simpliﬁed directed ﬁrst-passage percolation model. We use the Charlier ensemble to investigate the asymptotics of weakly increasing subsequences in random words and to prove a conjecture of Tracy and Widom. As a limit of the Meixner ensemble or the Charlier ensemble we obtain the Plancherel measure on partitions, and using this we prove a conjecture of Baik, Deift and Johansson that under the Plancherel measure, the distribution of the lengths of the ﬁrst k rows in the partition, appropriately scaled, converges to the asymptotic joint distribution for the k largest eigenvalues of a random matrix from the Gaussian Unitary Ensemble. In this problem a certain discrete kernel, which we call the discrete Bessel kernel, plays an important role.
ER  - 

