AB  - The link invariant, arising from the cyclic quantum dilogarithm via the particular R-matrix construction, is proved to coincide with the invariant of triangulated links in S3 introduced in [14]. The obtained invariant, like Alexander-Conway polynomial, vanishes on disjoint union of links. The R-matrix can be considered as the cyclic analog of the universal R-matrix associated with Uq(sl(2)) algebra. ENSLAPP-L-517/95 ∗On leave from St. Petersburg Branch of the Steklov Mathematical Institute, Fontanka 27, St. Petersburg 191011, RUSSIA †URA 14-36 du CNRS, associ´ee `a l’E.N.S. de Lyon, et `a l’Universit`e de Savoie
