AB  - We exhibit an inﬁnite family of knots with the property that the ﬁrst coeﬃcient of the n-colored Jones polynomial grows linearly with n. This shows that the concept of stability and tail seen in the colored Jones polynomials of alternating knots does not generalize naively.
