AB  - The implementation of tensor sources in Chiral Lagrangians allows the computation of Green functions and form factors involving tensor currents, that is, quark bilinears of the form ¯qi σ µν q j. Whereas only four new terms show up at O(p4), we ﬁnd around a hundred of them at O(p6). So it becomes essential to ensure that this set o operators is indeed minimal and non– redundant (i.e., it is a basis). We discuss two phenomenological applications in the context of vector meson resonances and the radiative pion decay.
