ID  - arxiv-1011.0679v2
AU  - OPDAM, ERIC
AU  - SOLLEVELD, MAARTEN
TI  - A FORMULA OF ARTHUR AND AFFINE HECKE ALGEBRAS
DA  - D:20210531
UR  - https://arxiv.org/abs/1011.0679
AB  - Let π, π′ be tempered representations of an aﬃne Hecke algebra with positive parameters. We study their Euler–Poincar´e pairing EP(π, π′), the alter- nating sum of the dimensions of the Ext-groups. We show that EP(π, π′) can be expressed in a simple formula involving an analytic R-group, analogous to a for- mula of Arthur in the setting of reductive p-adic groups. Our proof applies equally well to aﬃne Hecke algebras and to reductive groups over nonarchimedean local ﬁelds of arbitrary characteristic.
ER  - 

