ID  - arxiv-nucl-th-0409040v2
AU  - Platter∗, L.
TI  - On the correlation between the binding energies of the triton and the alpha-particle
DA  - D:20181112
UR  - https://arxiv.org/abs/nucl-th/0409040
AB  - We consider the correlation between the binding energies of the triton and the α-particle which is empirically observed in calculations employing diﬀerent phenomenological nucleon-nucleon in- teractions. Using an eﬀective quantum mechanics approach for short-range interactions with large scattering length |a| ≫ℓ, where ℓis the natural low-energy length scale, we construct the eﬀective interaction potential at leading order in ℓ/|a|. In order to renormalize the four-nucleon system, it is suﬃcient to include a SU(4)-symmetric one-parameter three-nucleon interaction in addition to the S-wave nucleon-nucleon interactions. The absence of a four-nucleon force at this order explains the empirically observed correlation between the binding energies of the triton and the α-particle. We calculate this correlation and obtain a prediction for the α-particle binding energy. Corrections to our results are suppressed by ℓ/|a|. PACS numbers: 21.45.+v, 21.10.Dr, 03.65.Ge ∗Electronic address: l.platter@fz-juelich.de †Electronic address: hammer@phys.washington.edu ‡Electronic address: meissner@itkp.uni-bonn.de
