ID  - arxiv-1210.5756v1
AU  - Reid‡, Károly Bezdek†and Samuel
TI  - Contact Graphs of Unit Sphere Packings Revisited ∗
DA  - D:20180508
UR  - https://arxiv.org/abs/1210.5756
AB  - The contact graph of an arbitrary ﬁnite packing of unit balls in Euclidean 3-space is the (simple) graph whose vertices correspond to the packing elements and whose two vertices are connected by an edge if the corresponding two packing elements touch each other. One of the most basic questions on contact graphs is to ﬁnd the maximum number of edges that a contact graph of a packing of n unit balls can have. In this paper, improving earlier estimates, we prove that the number of touching pairs in an arbitrary packing of n unit balls in E3 is always less than 6n−0.926n 2 3 . Moreover, as a natural extension of the above problem, we propose to study the maximum number of touching triplets (resp., quadruples) in an arbitrary packing of n unit balls in Euclidean 3-space. In particular, we prove that the number of touching triplets (resp., quadruples) in an arbitrary packing of n unit balls in E3 is at most 25 3 n (resp., 11 4 n).
ER  - 

TY  - JOUR
ID  - arxiv-1508.01627v4
TI  - REPRESENTATION THEORY An Electronic Journal of the American Mathematical Society (Xxxx XX, XXXX) S 1088-4165(XX)0000-0 A MURNAGHAN–NAKAYAMA RULE FOR VALUES OF UNIPOTENT CHARACTERS IN CLASSICAL GROUPS
DA  - D:20180919
UR  - https://arxiv.org/abs/1508.01627
AB  - We derive a Murnaghan–Nakayama type formula for the values of unipotent characters of ﬁnite classical groups on regular semisimple elements. This relies on Asai’s explicit decomposition of Lusztig restriction. We use our formula to show that most complex irreducible characters vanish on some ℓ-singular element for certain primes ℓ. As an application we classify the simple endotrivial modules of the ﬁnite quasi-simple classical groups. As a further application we show that for ﬁnite simple classical groups and primes ℓ≥3 the ﬁrst Cartan invariant in the principal ℓ-block is larger than 2 unless Sylow ℓ-subgroups are cyclic.
ER  - 

TY  - JOUR
ID  - arxiv-math-0606435v2
AU  - REPRESENTATIONS, AND OTHER LINK BRAID
TI  - arXiv:math/0606435v2 [math.GT] 10 Oct 2007
DA  - D:20130820
UR  - https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0606435
AB  - We show that 3-braid links with given (non-zero) Alexander or Jones polynomial are ﬁnitely many, and can be effectively determined. We classify among closed 3-braids strongly quasi-positive and ﬁbered ones, and show that 3-braid links have a unique incompressible Seifert surface. We also classify the positive braid words with Morton-Williams-Franks bound 3 and show that closed positive braids of braid index 3 are closed positive 3-braids. For closed braids on more strings, we study the alternating links occurring. In particular we classify those of braid index 4, and show that their Morton-Williams-Franks inequality is exact. Finally, we use the Burau representation to obtain new braid index criteria, including an efﬁcient 4-braid test.
ER  - 

